A better scheduling question is: **Which activities require another activity to finish, start, cool, thaw, or set first; which resources and the single operator can be used simultaneously; and which materials must be ready together before the next operation can begin?** Applied here, the PCR setup must precede cycling; agarose preparation begins 25 minutes after cycling starts and must cool before casting; the gel must set completely before entering the rig; ladder preparation begins 10 minutes after pouring; and loading waits for cycling to finish, the ladder to be ready, the gel to be in the rig, and the PCR products to be prepared. The polymerase remains cold until the last moment, but this is a handling condition rather than a separately timed activity, so no additional step is added.

